---
title: ":waffle: Sourdough Waffles or Pancakes"
source: https://littlespoonfarm.com/sourdough-pancakes-waffles-recipe/
author: Amy Duska
serves: 4
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 6 minutes
total time: 12 hours 16 minutes
tags:
  - breakfast
  - sourdough
  - waffle
  - pancake
---

In a large #mixing bowl{}, #whisk{} together @sourdough starter{200%g}(stirred down discard, 2/3 cup), @buttermilk{1%cup}(or milk), @granulated sugar{3%Tbsp}(or honey), @vanilla extract{1%tsp}, melted @butter{4%Tbsp}, and @all-purpose flour{2%cups} until well combined. Cover the bowl and let rest on the counter at room temperature overnight, or up to ~{12%hours}.

When ready to cook, add lightly beaten @eggs{2%large}, @baking soda{1%tsp}, @baking powder{1%tsp}, and @fine sea salt{1%tsp} to the batter, stir to combine, and cover the bowl. Let the batter rest for ~{20%minutes} at room temperature while the #waffle iron{} or #griddle{} preheats. (To cook the batter the same day without an overnight ferment, whisk all ingredients together in a large bowl and let rest for ~{20%minutes} before cooking.)

For waffles, preheat a #waffle iron{} and lightly grease with cooking oil spray. Pour 3/4 cup of batter into the center of the iron, gently spread the batter, and cook until golden brown or according to the manufacturer's directions, 3 to ~{6%minutes}. Makes 4 standard-sized waffles.

For pancakes, preheat a #griddle{} until very hot. Lightly grease the griddle and pour 1/4 cup of batter in a round shape onto the griddle. Cook until the bottom is golden brown and bubbles cover the top of the pancake, then flip and cook until cooked through and golden brown on both sides, about ~{3%minutes} per side. Makes about 12 pancakes.
